# Project Startup Fix

The project was failing to start due to a stale lock file and background processes from a previous session. I have resolved this by:

1.  **Terminating background processes**: Identified and killed existing `node` and `next-server` processes that were occupying the development environment.
2.  **Clearing the lock file**: Removed the [.next/dev/lock](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/proyecto%20inf_1/.next/dev/lock) file that was preventing a new instance of the dev server from starting.
3.  **Restarting the server**: Successfully initiated `npm run dev`.

## Project Status

The development server is now running and ready.

- **URL**: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
- **Status**: Ready in 714ms (Turbopack)

> [!NOTE]
> If you encounter this error again, you can usually fix it by running:
> `rm -f ".next/dev/lock"`

